\begin_layout Section
Motivation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thanks to enormous progress in the field of artificial intelligence, more
 and more problems can be taken over by machines.
 In the meantime it is not only possible to relieve humans of complex tasks
 but also to develop completely new solutions to problems, which is done
 in the field of Reinforcement Learning (RL).
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

RL is a part of ML where an agent without prior knowledge learns a strategy
 to maximise the expected reward in an environment.
 The environment represents a Markov decision process, which is a stochastic
 form of determinism in which the agent moves from one state, when performing
 an action, with a certain probability to the same subsequent state each
 time.
 The agent has only limited computing power at his disposal, which is why
 he must carefully weigh up exploration and exploitation in order to develop
 an efficient strategy.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
RL has become very popular due to the development of superhuman strategies,
 for example for the game Go.
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "AlphaGo_paper"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 This game was considered to be reserved for humans for a long time because
 of the deep understanding of positions and the enormously high possibility
 of possible moves.
 Through a clever arachitecture the team not only succeeded in beating a
 world star of the game with media impact, new techniques could even be
 observed.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Despite this extraordinary performance, the developers did not fully trust
 AlphaGo and therefore had the process monitored by a human.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quotation
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

It’s unbelieveably superhuman, in general, but it has some particular weaknesses
 in some situations.
 We can think of there being this space of all the things it knows about,
 and it knows about most of it extremely well.
 Then there will be these tricky lumps of knowledge, that it just understands
 very poorly.
 And it's really hard for us to characterize when it is going to enter into
 one of these lumps.
 But if it does, it can be completely delusional, thinking that it is alive
 on one part of the board when, in fact, it's dead or vice versa.
 So, there is a real risk that we could lose the match.
\begin_inset Quotes erd
