\begin_layout Standard
As described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "XAI_survey"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, a distinction is made between interpretability and explainability.
 Interpretability is defined as 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

the ability to explain or to present in understandable terms to humans
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and is thus based on the classic version of an explanation are 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

the details or reasons that someone gives to make something clear or easy
 to understand
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 [xxx quelle Cambridge Dictionary].
 Explicability is, in contrast, rather a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

collection of features of interpretable domain that have contributed for
 a given example to produce a decision
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
 An explanation should thus be provided for the gap between a person who
 has knowledge causally based on paradigms and an unmanageable, unknown
 logic, without relying solely on statistical tests.
 How explainable a solution is depends on the effort needed for a person
 to gain enough understanding to trust the approach.
 
\end_layout

