\begin_layout Standard
To trust applications in the industry, where small wrong decisions can often
 lead to big damages which can also be prosecuted in court for undesirable
 developments requires more robust explanations.
 It is therefore up to domain experts to find solution strategies in many
 areas.
 These solutions are trusted because the developer is trusted.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Large pool of qualified previous knowledge
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

In the case of complex problems, it is possible to build on the knowledge
 of the whole of mankind that has been safely acquired.
 In the case of a RL problem, it is always necessary to start from scratch,
 which is why there are many more potential sources of error.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Humans do not like to learn new stuff, but to simply use already learned
 strategies.
 Um eine Strategie zu entwickeln wird wo es geht bereits erlerntes Wissen
 eingesetzt.
 Hier kann der Mensch auch auf einen Ggroßen Wissensschatz zurückgreifen.
 A well-known example of such a mastered ability is the recognition of shapes
 and faces, which man perfected as a baby to such an extent that interpersonal
 explanations are no longer necessary, die im übrigen auch nicht teil einer
 Erklärung wären.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

due to the similar thought processes it is possible for humans to put themselves
 in another person's shoes and convey information in an even pedagogically
 valuable way.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Efficient and secure learning process, Implicit logic 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Humans have protective mechanisms at their disposal, which have developed
 through the evolutionary process of humans and accompany every learning
 process.
 Among other things, it enables us to recognize and avoid dangers, which
 requires caution and the recognition of causal relationships.
 We can therefore be sure that our entire pattern of action excludes life-threat
ening damage for us.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Computer sind, im Gegensatz zum Menschen, auf zufällige Exploration angewiesen,
 welche sowohl die Startparametrisierung sowie die Exploration beeinflussen.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Explicit logic through the formulation in a language
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Heuristics and explanations are formulated in already defined languages
 and can be checked for their truthfulness.
 
