\begin_layout Section
Evolutionary algorithms
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Evolutionary algorithms are metaheuristic optimization methods that optimize
 the genes of a population over generations using random mutation, crossover
 and a selection process between generations.
 They require two essential components:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Representation as genome (composition of genes)
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

These genes can be mutated or crossed between candidates so that the best
 ones survive in an evolutionary way over generations 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Koza_GP_1992,poli08:fieldguide_to_genetic_programming"
literal "true"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
