\begin_layout Plain Layout
AIs, a distinction is made between online and offline training.
 Online training means that the agent learns live and in the real environment,
 offline training means that the agent learns on a surrogate model, for
 example by regression on a data set.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Neuropolicies post-hoc ganzheitlich zu erklären ist eine Aufgabe, die aktuell
 nur verlustbehaftet möglich ist.
 As Daniel Hein has found out in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
after "p. 125"
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, policies that have been trained on offline data generated by a neuropolicy
 are almost always significantly worse than the neuropolicy or gp solutions
 that were trained on real system dynamics and thus could not further explain
 the neuropolicy.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
However, offline training still offers an interpretable and very cost-effective
 alternative which can also be trained risk-free.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
