\begin_layout Plain Layout
Starting from the origin (orange) and a target solution (green) there are
 several path candidates.
 In classical regression, only the deviation from the target solution is
 evaluated; path (1.) and path (2.) would be equally good here.
 Path (1.) achieves this, however, with a much smaller change in behaviour,
 which should be preferred from a confidence perspective.
 Path (3.) is not only worse, it is even worse in this area than the known
 solution.
 Areas where the expert solution is already close to the target solution
 should not be changed.
 Path (4.) deviates here at a point which was already well solved and therefore
 makes no sense.
 
