\begin_layout Subsection
Random tree branch building (node based)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In GP, the generation of random trees and branches is usually based on the
 tree depth.
 However, this is a problem for the layerwise mutation, where several branches
 have to be built up at the same time as the tree size can grow exponentially,
 the starting depth may differ between branches and the trees may end up
 very unbalanced.
 Therefore a node based algorithm was developed, which builds up branches
 in full- and grow mode up to a certain number of nodes without risk of
 structural imbalances.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float algorithm
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
n := goal amount of nodes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
b := amount of branches to build simultaneously
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
n = rand()  # n=80
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
tree_sizes = [n.split(min)]  # [15, 40, 25]
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
for nodes in [tree_sizes]:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout LyX-Code
while(True):
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout LyX-Code
for node in layer:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
